      "side": 0,
      "message": "i believe we should put some of these restrictions here in the user code rather than in libpldm++\n\n\u003e When ComponentOptions bit 1 is not set, this field should use the value of 0xFFFFFFFF.\n\n\u0027should\u0027, not \u0027shall\u0027\nhttps://www.iso.org/sites/directives/current/part2/index.xhtml#_idTextAnchor078\n\nmeaning the spec does not require it, so we either need parsing options or check this in user code.\n\nFor the `ComponentSize \u003d\u003d 0` i did not find anything in the spec. The image makes it look as if the component image is not empty and non-empty images create problems for user code.\n\nRegarding the `ComponentLocationOffset` validation, a patch for that is in the pipe:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/97009 . Thanks for finding these gaps 👍\n\nplanning to add the missing checks to the user code here with the next revision once the required `PackageVersionString` field and other metadata is provided by libpldm++",
